WEBVTT

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.360
Doesn't look like he's ready to get up yet.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.740
That's our research sample!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.410
If you take it, you'll be recognized as a devil,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.890
and you will suffer God's punishment!

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.580
Devil, huh?

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.180
I guess I wouldn't want to wake up, either.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.570
It'd be much nicer to stay in a dream.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.680
Watch out!

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.970
That hurt! What the hell was that for?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.680
That was close.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.600
Any longer and your perversion would have rubbed off on that boy.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.890
Rubbed off?!

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.560
So what's your plan?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.210
For what?

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.950
Isn't it obvious?

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:53.760
The child you abandoned has come all this way for your support.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.280
How do you intend to take responsibility as a father?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.850
Don't make up people's life stories!

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.330
You're being chased by Runa soldiers, too!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.810
If you skulk around too much...

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.280
There.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.900
I happened upon this. It had fallen by the side of the road, so I took it.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.910
Care for a lift?

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.000
<i>Happened upon it</i>?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.780
<i>By the side of the road</i>? <i>Fallen</i>?!

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.120
You clearly stole it from some nobles!

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.030
It doesn't matter! Put the boy inside.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.020
Hurry, or your perversion will rub off on him.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.090
Knock that off!

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.520
You're right, though. I can't carry him all the way to the town of Regit.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.070
So you went looking for a carriage?

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.220
You're surprisingly considerate.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.650
Now, Silver!

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.830
Ah! I haven't— Hey!

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.550
Ferris?!

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.020
Hi-ho, Silver!

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:53.530
Run at full speed, and flee that troublesome perverted man!

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.290
Hey, hold on!

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.810
Come on! Are you seriously leaving me in the dust?!

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:02.300
If you don't want to get left behind, then run! Run!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:07.760
You little— Cut the crap! Wait up, damn you!

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.720
Thank you. Set it right there.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.780
Please take a moment from work to eat it before it turns cold.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.320
Once I take care of this mountain of documents, I'll help myself.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.540
I understand that, but...

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.040
Ah. Here's a document from Claugh Klom, Field Marshal of the Roland Empire.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.160
You stuck me with this boring-ass job!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.510
I'm gonna kill you, Sion, you hear me?! I'm coming for you!

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:52.300
These are all documents submitted from those recently appointed to high posts.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.630
They seem to mostly be commoners.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.310
I wasn't exactly going out of my way to exclude nobles.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.170
It has nothing to do with birth.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.860
It's simply the result of making selections based on actual ability.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:08.020
Those people have offered this many proposals in just the past few days.

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.740
To build a better country...

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:14.500
To build a better life, this country is trying to make a fresh start.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.610
If that is so, it is all the more reason Your Majesty should consider his own health.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.960
Please, have it all.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.010
I suppose I will.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.960
Then, if you will excuse me.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:34.390
Trying to make a fresh start, hm? But...

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.050
It's too quiet.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.860
Will matters really end this way?

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.050
Enter.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.330
Was something the matter?

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.620
I've been informed that in the Arkmel region,

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.660
a general unrest among the nobles is growing.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.290
Arkmel.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.290
House Froaude's territory.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.530
Father.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.660
Ah, Miran.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.410
The guests are all gathered.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.620
Is that so?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.290
I'm quite impressed.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:42.530
One word from you, and renowned figures from all across the nation gather in one hall.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:45.620
Don't be silly. If not for your efforts,

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:45.630
this wouldn't have gone nearly so smoothly.
Don't be silly. If not for your efforts,

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.580
this wouldn't have gone nearly so smoothly.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:52.320
Not at all. My power is far from a match for yours, Father.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:55.100
You are my pride and joy, my son.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.270
Even raised with beauty and wisdom.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:03.060
You're always the best.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.110
Yes, the best...

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:13.740
I, too, consider it an honor to have been made your son, Father.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.730
Yes, yes...

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:19.610
Let us save the enjoyment for later.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:21.710
Our guests await.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.170
Thank you for your patience.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:33.840
My thanks to you all for your patronage.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.210
The organizers of tonight's banquet

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:40.240
are Duke Stearied, who is standing there,

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:44.320
and my father, Karlal Froaude.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:51.280
Ladies and gentlemen, I am grateful from the bottom of my heart

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.700
for your kind response to our invitation.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:59.290
And I'm certain all of you wise people are always aware...

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:05.340
...of why we are gathered here today.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.110
It's to kill that upstart brat, Sion Astal!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.390
Yes! How dare he slight us, the nobility?!

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.220
Have that man dethroned!

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.020
Indeed! Now is the time for us to take a stand.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.340
Royal lineage or not, he will never be more than the child of a lowborn cur.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:28.390
If we leave someone like that in charge, this country will be doomed!

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:30.780
Before that happens, we must crush him.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.520
The arrangements are in order.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.820
We will join hands with the Runa Empire, which was friendly with the late king,

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.020
and have Astal removed.

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:44.580
Miran came up with the plan, and he shall share the details.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:53.760
What's wrong, Miran?

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:07.270
First there is something that I would like all of those gathered here to do.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.650
Die, please.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.110
What is the meaning of this?!

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.490
Miran! What on earth—?

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.070
Let there be darkness!

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:46.170
What is the meaning of this, Miran?

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:49.780
You wouldn't— Even me?

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:53.850
I have long awaited this day, with eager anticipation.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.460
Ever since I came to you.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.020
From the very beginning, I have always had a place I needed to reach.

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:04.160
You are little more than a pawn I used for that purpose.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.260
U-Used? You lie!

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:11.110
When I first met you, you were only five years old!

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:15.210
At that time, the head of House Froaude was your older brother.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:21.470
But that brother and other family members all perished, one after another,

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.600
in unforeseen accidents.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.520
And you inherited all of House Froaude.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.010
You mean— You killed them?

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.270
The entire family?

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:38.370
Not yet. You still remain.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.280
W-Wait, Miran!

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:45.470
I have grown tired of hearing that voice of yours.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.790
Farewell, Father.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:47.800
S-Stop.
Farewell, Father.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.040
S-Stop.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:02.990
My gratitude for your cooperation, Duke Stearied.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:06.220
Thanks to you, I was able to make a clean sweep of all the elements of unrest.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:11.270
Please remember this. If you betray me—

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.100
I would never betray you!

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.760
Fighting against you?

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:17.570
I will never, ever defy y—

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:23.120
What was that?

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:42.300
You escaped my shadow and survived. Who on earth might you be?

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.720
The fact that I'm hear obviously means that I'm a Roland noble—

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.520
Surely you jest. That peach-colored hair...

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.440
There are none with hair that color here in the south of the continent.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.980
I see! You seem to be a pretty sharp man.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.280
What country might you hail from?

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.690
Do I look like the kind of man who would answer when asked that?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.570
I would like for you to answer me.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:07.580
Sorry, but I have one more job left to do.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.750
I didn't want to use too much power here,

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.960
but I guess I can't have it my way.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.130
Darkness—

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.590
Lightning Beasts!

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.840
Come forth!
Come forth!

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:27.850
As I thought. You carry a weapon similar to mine.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:31.310
"Ah, I don't want to fight you after all!"

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:35.560
This is the first time I've met someone who didn't react like that when they saw these Lightning Beasts.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.570
Nonetheless, I am highly surprised.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.400
Your very existence is outside my predictions.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.610
And you even killed Duke Stearied.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:49.790
Which in turn, would mean that someone was behind the duke, manipulating him.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.670
Someone connected to your country, who is here in Roland, if I am not mistaken?

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:57.630
Guess I should've just gotten out while the getting was good.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:01.130
But while I'm here, I'll be taking your ring!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.050
What I seek is the burning field!

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.060
Aw, hell! Lightning Beasts!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.980
An equal level of power, huh?!

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.310
Doesn't look like we'll be able to settle much at this rate!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.320
No, you must realize it by now.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.360
You cannot use magic.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.660
After all, if you did, it would reveal what country you were from.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.450
If the power of our rings is equal,

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:32.120
then I, the one who can use magic, have the advantage.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.080
Besides which—

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.660
You're still talking?

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.620
Every door in this hall is sealed shut.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:41.550
You would have to use these Lightning Beasts or whatever you call them to escape.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:45.220
However, the moment you turn one beast towards a door,

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.050
My beasts will devour your throat.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.220
You don't have many friends, do you?

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:54.350
I get that a lot. So, what will you do?

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.770
Will you give in?

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.100
Will you try to flee, knowing that you will be killed?

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:00.810
I'll pass on both choices.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:03.940
I've got one more option.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.150
An Iino Doue crystal!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.860
With this, I win!

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:14.410
This is—

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:46.780
By directing my shadows at the doors, I've weakened my rear defense.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.360
I've underestimated you.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:51.570
I never imagined I'd meet my end somewhere like this...

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.580
Get down!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.040
Field Marshal Klom?

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.250
Let's go!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.890
Why are you here?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.640
We'll talk later!

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.890
Let there be darkness!

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:25.820
Field Marshal Klom, my shadows will not hold for much longer.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:26.780
Leave this to me!

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.180
It seems we're safe.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.510
So, why were you here, Field Marshal Klom?

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.560
I came under orders from Sion, obviously!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.480
It's not like I wanted to come.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:05.440
His Majesty? But why would you come alone, given your Field Marshal position?

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.480
Of course I brought soldiers with me.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:12.320
Sion said there could be reprisals, and that it'd be dangerous to go alone.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:12.990
But—

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.490
Going off and doing your own thing in secret?

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:20.580
When I think of your face, it makes me want to punch it!

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.120
I just came alone ahead of the others.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:28.050
How odd. You just said that you didn't wish to come here.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:30.050
Yet, you even left soldiers behind to—

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:34.180
I told you, I wanted to punch your face in, so I rushed it!

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:37.260
And you rescued me without even hitting me.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.640
You're a difficult man to comprehend, you know. Quite an odd one.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.060
I don't want to hear that from you!

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.230
You have my gratitude nonetheless.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.360
I would have certainly been dead, the way things were going.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.980
You saved me.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:52.190
What was that blue flame?

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.200
What the hell's going on?

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.870
I do not know. However...

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:59.620
...it seems that our war...

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.620
...has already begun.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.880
are currently headed to the castle.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.510
Good work. You may leave.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:16.470
Sir!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:25.640
It won't work.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.690
My, what an interesting attack.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.650
Beasts of lightning, hm?

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.070
But interesting is all it is.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.780
Before me, nothing will work.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:45.910
But if you still seek to make a move on this country's king...

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:49.080
...you will end up disappearing.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.460
Feel free to tell your companions as well

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.920
what happens to those who raise a hand against Roland.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.840
His presence has vanished. He seems to have fled.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:01.720
Should we have captured him?

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.930
That is for you to decide.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:07.600
If you wish it, I can still go capture him.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.230
No, leave it at that.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:14.780
Yes, you're still fine. You still haven't broken.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.320
An era of upheaval is coming, is it not?

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:21.990
But with you as king, I believe that our country can still survive it.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:25.120
And if I cannot protect this kingdom?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.370
I will kill you and crown a new, more competent king.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:33.590
So until that point, you may do as you please.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.460
As I please, hm?

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.220
Something has begun to happen.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:40.470
Something...

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.800
The sword family, huh?

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:46.890
Yeesh, this country's nothing but a bunch of veritable monsters.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.230
I screwed up my job, too.

00:18:55.820 --> 00:19:00.320
See, our king... He told us to join hands with the Runa Empire.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.030
You won't say no, right?

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:06.290
Our Runa Empire is already allied with Roland!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.870
You conspired with the nobles of Roland,

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:13.000
to overthrow Roland's current king, didn't you?

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:19.420
But your contact, Duke Stearied, has been killed by our companion.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:24.260
Which means that you can't aim for Roland any longer.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:28.140
Now then, I'll ask you once more, Your Majesty.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.770
Would you join hands with us?

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.650
With the Gastark Empire?

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.320
Well, I'll give you some time to think it over.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.400
We have other work to do.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.200
We'll be looking forward to your response.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.240
So, Kuu. Where were we headed next?

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.580
You forgot?! For crying out loud!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.960
That's why I can't get separated from you, brother Sui!

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.830
It's about time you stood on your own!

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.040
S-Sorry, Kuu.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:59.300
Okay, remember on your own! Do it in five seconds!

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.010
Five. Four.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.170
Er, uh, uhm...
Five. Four.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:01.970
Three. Two.
Er, uh, uhm...

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.640
It was some village, right?
Three. Two.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.100
The town of Regit!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:14.480
Geez, they don't know when to quit!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.230
Hurry, they're catching up.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:21.150
You seriously pricked me just now!

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.700
Come, dance! Keep dancing the sinner's dance!

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.450
You little—

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.080
You devil!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.460
Do you think a monster can flee in the face of our God?!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.170
What god? That's such crap.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:37.840
I implore our God who dwells in Heaven

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:41.800
to bestow upon thy pitiful servants a blade of ice to destroy demons!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.680
I offer up this contract,

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.970
to unleash the magic beast of light which dances through the skies!

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:55.100
Yo! How's Arua?

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:56.900
Still asleep.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.020
Are you really returning to the town of Regit?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:02.740
Yeah. We'd better take that Kuku girl with us, too.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.990
Take her with us?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:08.580
As long as they're in that town, Arua and that girl won't be happy.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:11.410
We should take them someplace where they can live quietly in peace.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.630
We've got more pursuers. Quit slacking.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.170
Come. Dance, dance, dance!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:22.960
Hey! Quit it! Come on! Who... said I had to—

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.720
That hurts!

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.850
Is entry inspection very complicated?

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:40.980
Fool! There's no way Imperial Stohl would lose to a puny country like that!

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:46.780
Roland... Cassla... Estolia... Stohl...

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.570
Next!

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:49.910
Coming!

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:25.500
<i>Look, I'm getting real sick of all these shitty things happening everywhere.</i>

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:28.260
<i>The north of the continent? Gastark?</i>

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:30.930
<i>I'm not bothering with a country that far off!</i>

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.350
<i>It sucks that they came out this way at all!</i>
